1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:03,556
Part twenty. Backup and data safety.

2
00:00:04,410 --> 00:00:06,876
Open Settings, Backup and data.

3
00:00:06,876 --> 00:00:11,968
Download backup saves one file with all records, attached files,

4
00:00:11,968 --> 00:00:16,583
your staff list without passwords, and document numbering.

5
00:00:16,583 --> 00:00:21,356
Do it every week and keep it on Google Drive or a pen drive.

6
00:00:22,250 --> 00:00:27,792
Restore from backup puts a backup back, also on a new phone or computer.

7
00:00:27,792 --> 00:00:32,796
Staff from the backup are added; set their passwords under Users.

8
00:00:32,796 --> 00:00:37,183
Invoice numbers already given out are never issued again.

9
00:00:38,090 --> 00:00:42,331
The app also keeps safety copies by itself: every day,

10
00:00:42,331 --> 00:00:45,315
before an update and before a restore.

11
00:00:45,315 --> 00:00:49,712
If something goes wrong, go back to a copy with Restore.

12
00:00:50,610 --> 00:00:56,726
To try every screen, load the demo data of a sample solar company; your own data is

13
00:00:56,726 --> 00:01:00,484
kept aside and comes back when you remove the demo.

14
00:01:00,484 --> 00:01:06,453
In cloud mode, everything lives in one secure online database for the whole team.

15
00:01:07,620 --> 00:01:11,031
Next video: Using SuryaSetu on your phone.

